## 3. Group Role Permissions for Member Users

Implement role-based permissions for member users.

Use the following baseline permission model, adapting it to existing functionality where necessary.

| Action | Owner | Admin | Moderator | Member |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| View accessible group | Yes | Yes | Yes | Yes |
| Manage group settings | Yes | Yes | No | No |
| Manage group members | Yes | Yes | Limited | No |
| Change member roles | Yes | Limited | No | No |
| Assign or remove owners | Yes | No | No | No |
| Perform moderation actions | Yes | Yes | Yes | No |
| Join or leave groups | Subject to owner safeguards | Yes | Yes | Yes |
| Archive or delete a group | Yes | Limited/No | No | No |

Interpretation and additional rules:

- All owners have equal permissions.
- Owners can manage group settings, members, roles, and ownership.
- Group admins can manage routine group settings and membership, but cannot promote themselves to owner, remove or demote owners, or change ownership.
- Moderators can perform the existing supported moderation actions but cannot manage group settings or roles.
- Members have ordinary group participation permissions.
- All member actions must also respect group visibility, membership status, and applicable business rules.
- An owner must not be able to leave, be removed, or be demoted if doing so would leave the group without an owner.
- When transferring ownership, validate the operation and ensure that at least one owner remains.
- If multiple owners exist, one owner must not receive greater permissions merely because they were the first owner.

If an existing feature uses different role terminology or permission semantics, inspect it and reconcile the implementation consistently rather than introducing conflicting rules.

